th=2 /></svg></div></div><div class=mobile-dropdown-options id=mobile-dropdown-options><a href=/legal/deposit-agreement-cbw class=mobile-dropdown-option>Deposit Agreement - CBW</a> <a href=/legal/deposit-agreement-evolve class=mobile-dropdown-option>Deposit Agreement - Evolve</a> <a href=/legal/deposit-agreement-continental class=mobile-dropdown-option>Deposit Agreement - Continental</a> <a href=/legal/loan-disclosures class=mobile-dropdown-option>Disclosures</a> <a href=/legal/electronic-signatures-and-communications class=mobile-dropdown-option>Electronic Signatures and Communications</a> <a href=/legal/privacy-policy class=mobile-dropdown-option>Privacy Policy</a><div class="mobile-dropdown-option active"data-tab=terms-of-use>Terms of Use</div><a href=/legal/loan-disclosures class=mobile-dropdown-option>Loan Disclosures</a></div></div></div><div class=legal-sidebar><nav class=legal-nav><a href=/legal/deposit-agreement-cbw class=legal-nav-item>Deposit Agreement - CBW </a><a href=/legal/deposit-agreement-evolve class=legal-nav-item>Deposit Agreement - Evolve </a><a href=/legal/deposit-agreement-continental class=legal-nav-item>Deposit Agreement - Continental </a><a href=/legal/disclosures class=legal-nav-item>Disclosures </a><a href=/legal/electronic-signatures-and-communications class=legal-nav-item>Electronic Signatures and Communications </a><a href=/legal/privacy-policy class=legal-nav-item>Privacy Policy </a><a href=# class="legal-nav-item active">Terms of Use </a><a href=/legal/loan-disclosures class=legal-nav-item>Loan Disclosures</a></nav></div><div class=legal-content><div class=legal-content-header><h2 class=legal-content-title>Bright Money Terms of Use</h2></div><div class=legal-full-content><div class=legal-section><div class=legal-text><p>Last Updated: October 03, 2025<p>This Bright Money Terms of Use (this "Agreement") is provided by Bright Capital Inc. ("Bright Money," "we," "us" or "our"), and governs your use of our App and Services. <span style=text-decoration:underline>THIS AGREEMENT CONTAINS A BINDING ARBITRATION PROVISION THAT MAY BE ENFORCED BY THE PARTIES AND A WAIVER OF YOUR CLASS ACTION RIGHTS.</span><p><strong>Privacy Notice</strong><br>At Bright Money, user privacy is an important concern. We are committed to maintaining privacy and security, and to providing the best possible user experience. We also strive to protect the personal and confidential information of those who use our services. <a href=/legal/privacy-policy style=color:#0e1e14;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600;color:inherit>Click here</a> for our entire Privacy Policy. This policy may be updated by us from time to time, so please check here frequently.<p>You authorize your wireless carrier to use or disclose information about your account and your wireless device, if available, to Bright Money or its service provider for the duration of your business relationship, solely to help them identify you or your wireless device and to prevent fraud. See our <a href=/legal/privacy-policy style=color:#0e1e14;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600;color:inherit>Privacy Policy</a> for how we treat your data.<p>In general, you can visit <a href=https://www.brightmoney.co style=color:#0e1e14;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600;color:inherit>www.brightmoney.co</a> without telling us who you are or revealing any information about yourself. However, when you use the App or our Services, register for an account with us, or add a Linked Account, we will collect personal information from you, such as your name, email address, mobile phone number, banking, and credit card information, age, gender, location, address, date of birth, Social Security number, citizenship information, occupation status, and income source.<p>The personal information we collect may include the type of device in use, operating system, the device identifier, user's IP address, mobile network information, and standard web log information, such as your browser type, traffic to and from our App, the pages you accessed on our App, and other available information. We may also collect information about your use of our App.<p>By providing your personal information to us, you expressly agree to our collection, use, storage, and disclosure of such information as described in our <a href=/legal/privacy-policy style=color:#0e1e14;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600;color:inherit>Privacy Policy.</a><br>If you are dissatisfied with any aspect of the services you have received from Bright Capital Inc, you can send a complaint to <a href=mailto:complaints@brightmoney.co style=color:#0e1e14;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600;color:inherit>complaints@brightmoney.co</a>. We will review the complaint and provide you with a response in writing.<p>Terms of Use<br>Please read this Agreement carefully before using our services (the "Services") provided through our Bright Money App available in the App Store and on Google Play (the "App"). We may also provide the Services through the Bright Money Website (the "Website"), and if you access the Services through the Website, then all references to "App" in this Agreement include the Bright Money Website. This Agreement is between Bright Money and you, the user. By installing, accessing, or using the Services or the App by accepting electronically (for example, clicking "I Agree"), you agree to be bound by this Agreement, including our Privacy Policy.<p><strong>Changes to Terms of Service</strong><p>We may modify this Agreement at any time at our sole discretion. If we do so, we will notify you by posting the modified Agreement on the Bright Money App or Website with a new revision date, or through other communication channels such as email. It is important that you review this Agreement whenever we modify it because by continuing to use the Services after we have posted the modified Agreement, you are confirming to us that you agree to be bound by the modified terms. If you do not agree to the modified Agreement, then you may not use the Services or the App.<p>Use of Services<br>Your use of the App and Services is subject to the additional disclaimers and notices that may appear throughout the App. By installing, accessing, or using the Services or the App, and by accepting electronically (for example, by clicking "I Agree"), you agree to be bound by this Agreement and our Privacy Policy, and any modifications that we may make going forward. If you do not agree to this Agreement, then you may not use the Services or the App.<p>Neither Bright Money nor its representatives are engaged in rendering legal services, financial advice, or investment advice through the Services or the App.<p>Neither our Services nor the material on the App should be regarded as legal services, financial advice, investment advice, or an offer to sell, or a solicitation of an offer to buy, any securities of Bright Money or its affiliates.<p>Bright Money and its representatives assume no responsibility for any consequence relating directly or indirectly to any action or inaction based on the information, services, or other material on the App. While we strive to keep the information on the App accurate, complete, and up-to-date, Bright Money and its representatives cannot guarantee, and will not be responsible for any damage or loss related to, the accuracy, completeness, or timeliness of the information or the Services on the App.<p>Personal and Noncommercial Use Limitation: Prohibited Uses<br>Our Services, including the App, provide software tools and information to assist you in managing your finances and debt. We grant you access to the App during the term of this Agreement solely to receive the Services. You may access, download, and print materials as necessary to receive the Services. You may not license, copy, distribute, create derivative works from, frame in another Web page, use on any other website, or sell any information, databases, or lists obtained from the Services or the App. You agree to provide true, accurate, and complete user information at all times, and to update such information upon our request. You will not access or attempt to access password-protected, secure, or non-public areas of the Services or the App, without our prior written permission. You will comply with all privacy laws.<p>The Services and the App are licensed (not sold) to end-users. Subject to this Agreement, we grant to you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, limited, and revocable license to access the Services and the App for your personal use and not for any commercial or business purpose ("Your License").<p>Proprietary Rights<br>All materials on the Services and the App (as well as the organization and layout of the Services and the App) are owned and copyrighted, licensed by, or used with permission that is granted to Bright Money. No reproduction, distribution, or transmission of the copyrighted materials in the Services and the App are permitted without the prior written permission of Bright Money.<br>Your account<br>If you use the Services or the App, you are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of your account and password and for restricting access to your access device (such as your mobile device or computer), and you agree to accept responsibility for all activities that occur under your account or password. If your status as a user of the Services or the App is terminated, you will (i) stop using the Services and the App and any information obtained from the Services and the App, and (ii) destroy all copies of your account information, password and any information obtained from the Services or the App.<p>If you become aware of any unauthorized use of your account with us, you agree to notify us immediately at the email address: <a href=mailto:support@brightmoney.co style=color:#0e1e14;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600;color:inherit>support@brightmoney.co</a>.<br>Description of Bright Money's Services<br>Products & services are subject to state residency & regulatory requirements. Approval for Bright Credit is also subject to credit underwriting.<p>The Services allow you to track and organize your credit card debt. The Services currently are provided to you by Bright Money ("Basic Membership"). Bright Money also offers premium Membership ("Premium Membership") that allow you to access additional features in the App.<p>In order to enroll for the Services, you will need to sign up for an account with Bright Money on the App. We will verify your identity. You authorize us to make any inquiries we consider necessary to validate your identity, including, if requested, your full address, your date of birth, your Social Security number, and/or requiring you to take steps to confirm ownership of your email address or financial instruments, ordering a credit report, or verifying information you provide against third party databases or through other sources. If you do not provide this information or Bright Money cannot verify your identity, we will refuse to allow you to use the Services and the App.<p>Once you have established an account with us, you may link accounts or information as described below, and we will receive Account Information from the Data Aggregators (as defined below). We will analyze this Account Information and provide you a summary of our analysis so that you can develop a plan to make one or more payments on your credit card debt.<p>Bright Money is not an advisor, broker, credit repair company, or credit reporting agency. Our Services are not sponsored or endorsed by any third party.<p>Bright Money does not guarantee that the Services or any of its features will always be free, and reserves the right, in its sole discretion, to change at any time the pricing and availability of the Services or any feature of the Services.<p><strong>Membership Features and Pricing</strong><p>Bright Money offers Premium Memberships for our Services for a fee. Premium Membership allows you to unlock features and allow for reporting which features are unavailable through the Basic Services ("Premium Features"). Details regarding Premium Membership and Premium Features are available in the App, and are subject to change from time to time as outlined in this Agreement. Premium Memberships are available, at your choice, on a monthly, quarterly, half-yearly or annual term, and pricing may differ based on your choice of term. You can request to be switched to different plans and terms, at the time of their Membership or at the time of renewal. If we are unable to collect your membership fees, your plan will change from Premium Membership to Basic Membership.<p>Bright Money hereby reserves the right to modify Membership fees or introduce new charges at its discretion. Bright Money may change its pricing from time to time, and pricing updates will take effect at the beginning of your next term (i.e., the following month or the following year, depending upon the term you choose). All such changes and modifications will be updated on App and same shall reflect on App and continued usage of the App post the same shall be considered as consent to such changes and modifications. Any such alterations shall be communicated to you via electronic mail, providing a minimum notice period of 30 days from the effective date of the changes.<p>If you are on a Basic Membership and have a non-zero balance in your Bright Accounts, a monthly Membership Administrative Fee of $11 will be incurred. These fees will apply 30 days from the date your Premium Membership is downgraded to Basic either due to cancellation or automatic step-down to Basic Membership. If you withdraw funds from your Bright Accounts before the 30-day period is complete, no fees will be incurred. Funds can be withdrawn via the Bright App or by contacting Bright Customer Support.<p><strong>Automatic step down to lower plan</strong><p>If you purchase a Premium Membership, it will automatically renew for another term of the same length at a stepped down price in the event that the payment for the original plan is not auto-debited from the day it falls due.<p>This will not apply in the event that you opt to cancel your Membership to all Services before the current term runs out.<p>If we cannot collect payment for Premium Membership you will automatically step down to the Basic Membership tier.<p><strong>Optional step down to lower Plan</strong><p>Or you can opt for the lower priced plan at any time by sending us an email at <a href=mailto:support@brightmoney.co style=color:#0e1e14;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600;color:inherit>support@brightmoney.co</a> with the subject line: Step Down Plan.<p><strong>Premium Price Plans:</strong><ul style=list-style-type:disc;padding-left:20px;font-size:16px;color:#0e1e14><li>Annual plan $97 USD<li>6 month plan $68 USD<li>3 month plan $39 USD<li>1 month plan $14 USD<li>1 month plan $5 USD without Smart Round Ups</ul><p><strong>Basic Membership Administrative Fee:</strong> $11 (incurred for maintaining a non-zero balance on your Bright Accounts in Basic tier. This includes all accounts opened for associated Bright products or services with a non-zero balance.)<p><strong>Cancellation of Premium Membership</strong><p>If you still wish to cancel your Premium Membership, you can do so at any time via the App or by reaching out to us on email/chat. Bright Money is dedicated to ensuring that you have the flexibility to manage your Membership as per your requirements and needs.<p>The cancellation will take effect immediately or after expiry of the last day of the current Membership term based upon your choice. you will have to specify if you want immediate cancellation on the email to <a href=mailto:support@brightmoney.co class=underline-text style=color:#0e1e14;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600;color:inherit>support@brightmoney.co</a> else the automatic cancellation will take effect on the last date of Membership term.<p>In the event that you choose to cancel your Premium Membership, you will step down to Basic Membership until you delete your account.<p><strong>Refund for Membership Fees</strong><p>Any refunds due to you when you opt for a lower priced plan prior to expiry of current plan, will be processed within 14 days.<p>In the event that you cancel your Premium Membership less than 30 days from the start of your membership, refunds will be issued on a prorated basis provided you are on a non-monthly plan (quarterly, semi-annually or annually).<p>You agree and acknowledge that you are not eligible for any refund for any Membership term post the 14 days of payment towards Membership<p><strong>Rent Reporting Membership Policy</strong><p>Bright Money offers Rent Reporting services as part of the Premium membership for an add-on one-time fee of $35 (For reporting up to 24 months of your past payments) and a $4 monthly fee (For reporting payments of ongoing months) [Kindly note that this fee is in addition to Premium services charges]. Bright Rent Reporting includes reporting Rent payments based on eligibility. Bright does not guarantee reporting of your rent payments if you have opted in for the Rent Reporting Add-on.<p>Details regarding Premium Membership and Premium Features are available in the App and are subject to change from time to time as outlined in the Membership terms and conditions. With continued usage of the membership and features post change in terms and conditions will be construed as implicit acceptance of the revised terms and conditions.<p>Bright Money hereby reserves the right to charge the Rent Reporting Add-on fee of $35 (for past reporting) and $4 (for monthly reporting) if you have opted-in to the Rent Reporting add-on (Past and Monthly) in addition to your Bright Membership. Bright DOES NOT claim eligibility or approval for Rent Reporting services. Bright has the discretion to charge the add-on fee of $35 (for past reporting) and $4 (for monthly reporting) even if a customer has not completed the Rent Reporting application or has not been approved by Bright. Bright provides regular communications to complete the application and complete your approval for Rent Reporting via both emails and the Bright App.<p>Bright Premium membership is mandatory to avail of Rent Reporting services. If you cancel your Bright Membership your Rent Reporting services will be disabled. If we are unable to collect your Premium membership fees, your plan will change from Premium Membership to Basic Membership. This will also cause your Rent Reporting services to be disabled. You can resume your services by reactivating your Bright Premium Membership.<p>If you wish to only cancel your Rent Reporting services, you can do so by sending us an email at <a href=mailto:support@brightmoney.co class=underline-text style=color:#0e1e14;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:600;color:inherit>support@brightmoney.co</a> with the subject line: "Cancel Rent Reporting Services"<p><strong>Rent Reporting Refund Policy</strong><p>Bright Rent Reporting Refunds are handled separately from your Premium Membership refunds outlined in the Refunds terms and conditions. In the event that you cancel your Premium Membership less than 30 days from the start of your Bright Premium membership, refunds will be issued on a prorated basis.<p>You agree and acknowledge that you are not eligible for any refund for Rent Reporting Services post 14 days of payment towards Rent Reporting Membership (both past and monthly reporting).</div></div></div></div></div></section></div></div></section><section><div class="w-embed"><style>.page-wrapper{max-width:1920px;margin:0 auto;width:100%}</style><div class=page-wrapper><section id=legal-text-part2-section><div class=legal-container style=padding-top:0><div class=mobile-dropdown-container style=display:none><div class=mobile-dropdown-category></div><div class=mobile-dropdown-wrapper><div class=mobile-dropdown-button id=mobile-dropdown-btn-part2><div class=mobile-dropdown-content style=overflow:visible;margin-left:1rem;margin-top:0><span class=mobile-dropdown-text id=mobile-dropdown-text-part2></span></div><div class=mobile-dropdown-arrow id=mobile-dropdown-arrow-part2><svg fill=none height=24 viewBox="0 0 24 24"width=24><path d="M8 11L12 15L16 11"stroke=currentColor stroke-linecap=round stroke-linejoin=round stroke-width=2 /></svg></div></div><div class=mobile-dropdown-options id=mobile-dropdown-options-part2><a href=/legal/deposit-agreement-cbw class=mobile-dropdown-option></a> <a href=/legal/deposit-agreement-cbw class=mobile-dropdown-option></a> <a href=/legal/deposit-agreement-continental class=mobile-dropdown-option></a><div class="mobile-dropdown-option active"></div><a href=/legal/electronic-signatures-and-communications class=mobile-dropdown-option></a> <a href=/legal/privacy-policy class=mobile-dropdown-option></a> <a href=/legal/terms-of-use class=mobile-dropdown-option></a> <a href=/legal/loan-disclosures class=mobile-dropdown-option></a></div></div></div><div><div class=legal-sidebar><nav class=legal-nav><a href=/legal/deposit-agreement-cbw class=legal-nav-item></a> <a href=/legal/deposit-agreement-evolve class=legal-nav-item></a> <a href=/legal/deposit-agreement-continental class=legal-nav-item></a> <a href=/legal/disclosures class=legal-nav-item></a> <a href=/legal/electronic-signatures-and-communications class=legal-nav-item></a> <a href=/legal/privacy-policy class=legal-nav-item></a> <a href=# class="legal-nav-item active"></a> <a href=/legal/loan-disclosures class=legal-nav-item></a></nav></div></div><div class=legal-content><div class=legal-full-content><div class=legal-section><div class=legal-text><p><strong>Account Linking Terms</strong><p>By linking any of your accounts (each, a "Linked Account") or information held by us or any third parties to the Services, you authorize and direct us and/or our Data Aggregators (defined below) to access third party sites, databases, and other services relating to the Linked Account, to access, retrieve and use your account information or other information you direct us to access on an ongoing basis ("Account Information"). We may use the services of a third party to access your Account Information (these third parties are referred to as "Data Aggregators"). In some situations, this may include (i) authorizing us (either directly or through our Data Aggregator) to share your account login credentials or other information and (ii) granting us (either directly or through our Data Aggregator) full power and authority to take any additional steps, all as necessary to access, retrieve, and use your Account Information in accordance with this Agreement and our Privacy Policy. You acknowledge and agree that (a) when we or our Data Aggregator access, retrieve and use Account Information, we are acting as your agent, and not as the agent of or on behalf of any other party; (b) if we use a Data Aggregator to access your Account Information, that Data Aggregator will provide to us, on your behalf, your Account Information for our use in connection with the Service, including to respond to your inquiries, fulfill your requests, provide you with customer service, and identify offers from us and third parties that may be of interest to you; (c) we and our Data Aggregator may each use, modify, display, distribute, and create new material using your Account Information to offer Products to you and as otherwise described in our Privacy Policy; and (d) we and our Data Aggregator may each use, sell, license, reproduce, modify, distribute, and disclose aggregate or non-personally identifiable information derived through your use of the Services, including any Account Information obtained pursuant to the authorization above, for any purpose. Please refer to our <a href=/legal/privacy-policy class=underline-text style=color:inherit>Privacy Policy</a> for information on how we use, maintain, and share your Account Information.<p>We are not obligated to review Account Information for any purpose, including accuracy, legality, or non-infringement. You agree that we and our Data Aggregator shall be entitled to rely on the foregoing authorization granted by you. If you wish to revoke the foregoing authorization for any Linked Account, you must unlink the account from the Services and, if no other Linked Account is provided by you, you may not be able to receive the Services.<p>You represent and warrant you are a legal owner of the Linked Account, or that you are authorized to provide us and our Data Aggregator with all Account Information and have the right to grant the permissions in this Agreement with respect to the Linked Account, and that Data Aggregator's exercise of its rights in this Agreement will not violate any applicable laws or third party rights.<p>Bright may make up to two micro credit and debit transactions of $0.01 each per month to verify the active status of your linked checking account. The corresponding credit and debit transactions will net to zero, so there is no net change on your account balance after the transactions.<p>These transactions are initiated if there has been no activity with Bright in the past 30 days. We use your recent transaction data to build the most accurate AI plan for budgeting and debt-payoff. These micro-transactions help ensure your account is up to date, allowing Bright to deliver money insights and recommendations.<p>You can opt-out of these micro-transactions anytime by contacting us at <a href=mailto:support@brightmoney.co style=font-weight:700;text-decoration:underline;color:inherit>support@brightmoney.co</a>.<p><strong>Account Information Authorization</strong><p>As described in the "Account Linking Terms" section, above, you understand that, in connection with our Services, you authorize us to obtain certain Account Information about your Linked Accounts such as your credit card number, directly from you or from third parties (including Data Aggregators and Credit Bureaus). You also understand that we will – directly or through third parties to our Services – hold, maintain, and use your Account Information, as described above and consistent with our Privacy Policy, as long as is necessary to perform the Services.<p><strong>Credit Report Authorization</strong><p>You understand and agree that, in connection with our Services, you authorize us to send on your behalf information about you to one or more Data Aggregators and to obtain consumer reports and related information about you from one or more consumer reporting agencies, such as TransUnion, Experian, and Equifax. You also authorize lending partners to conduct a credit pull from the various credit reporting agencies in order for the lenders to make a credit decision on your application for financing.<p><strong>Smart Round-Up Deposits</strong><p>By enabling <strong>Smart Round-Ups</strong> in the Bright Money App, you authorize Bright Money to securely access and analyze transactions from your linked checking account (“Funding Account”) to calculate and accumulate small savings amounts (“Smart Round-Ups”). Bright Money will round up transactions to the nearest ten cents ($0.10) or may make micro-savings transfers of one to ten cents ($0.01–$0.10) several times a day, up to a maximum total of one dollar ($1.00) per day. The exact parameters of your Round-Ups settings, including micro-savings amounts and the daily maximum, can be modified in the Bright Money App. You are responsible for carefully reviewing your settings to your preferences. Smart Round-Ups will execute multiple daily electronic funds transfer (ACH debit) from your Funding Account to your Bright Stash Account for deposit per the Round-Ups ACH Authorization.<p>Funds transferred through Smart Round-Ups are deposited into your <strong>Bright Stash Account</strong>, held by Bright Money’s partner banks — <strong>Evolve Bank & Trust and Continental Bank</strong>, Members FDIC. Bright Money is not a bank and does not itself hold your funds. Smart Round-Ups funds may be used toward goals you set in the App, such as paying down credit cards, building savings, or funding Bright Builder (if applicable). If you are enrolled in Bright Builder, Round-Ups funds will first be applied toward your Builder security deposit until it is fully funded, after which future Round-Ups will be deposited in your Bright Stash Account.<p>You may access, withdraw, or transfer Smart Round-Ups funds at any time through the App and may pause, modify, or terminate participation in Smart Round-Ups whenever you choose. Smart Round-Ups are included in Premium Bright Membership, and Bright Money does not charge a separate fee for this feature. Your Funding Account institution may assess overdraft or insufficient-funds fees if it lacks available funds when a transfer occurs. You are solely responsible for maintaining sufficient funds in your Funding Account to cover all deposits and Round-Ups. Such fees are not collected or imposed by Bright Money and are solely your responsibility.<p>Bright Money <strong>may suspend or terminate Smart Round-Ups for compliance, security, or operational reasons (including insufficient funds, inactivity, or suspected unauthorized use). Any remaining balance in your Bright Stash Account will remain available to you in accordance with the account terms provided by the partner bank</strong>. Any remaining balance in your Bright Stash Account will remain available to you in accordance with the account terms provided by the partner bank.<p><strong>Bright Plan</strong><p>By enrolling in Bright Plan through the Bright Money App, you authorize Bright Money to access and analyze your linked financial accounts to generate personalized recommendations for budgeting, debt repayment, and savings management (“Bright Plan”). Bright Plan uses data from your linked accounts, spending patterns, and credit profile to provide insights and suggested actions that may include payment scheduling, savings targets, and credit-utilization awareness.<p>Bright Plan is an educational and informational tool designed to help you make decisions regarding the repayment of credit obligations and to improve your financial awareness. The suggestions, projections, or insights provided by Bright Plan are for educational purposes only and do not constitute financial, investment, legal, or a recommendation for debt repayment, credit counseling, or credit servicing. Bright Plan does not algorithmically execute any financial actions on your behalf, and no fiduciary, advisory, or counseling relationship exists between you and Bright Money. Customers can modify or change their Plan at any time, and remain solely responsible for all financial decisions and actions they take based on the information provided.<p>You may modify or discontinue your participation in Bright Plan at any time through the App. Bright Plan is included in Bright Membership at no additional charge. Bright Money may update, suspend, or discontinue Bright Plan features at any time for operational, compliance, or security reasons.<p>
                            <strong>
