                            We have established a relationship with Continental Bank, Member FDIC ("Continental Bank"). By completing the requested tasks and subject to the approval of Continental Bank, you can open a deposit account with Continental Bank. The Continental Bank deposit account is governed by the following documents: Customer Account Terms, which can be found by <a href="/legal/deposit-agreement-continental" style="color: inherit; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline; ">clicking here</a>; the Bright Capital, Inc Electronic Communication Consent, which can be found by <a href="/legal/electronic-signatures-and-communications" style="color: inherit; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline;">clicking here</a>; and the Continental Bank Privacy Notice, which can be found by <a href="/legal/privacy-policy" style="color: inherit; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline;">clicking here</a>. By opening your Continental Bank deposit account or by requesting a transfer to or from your Continental Bank deposit account, you agree to the terms of that deposit account as established by Continental Bank. Bank services are provided by Continental Bank. To report a complaint related to the bank services provided by Continental Bank, call us at <a href="tel:1-877-274-6494" style="font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline; cursor: pointer; color: #0E1E14;">1-877-274-6494</a>  or visit <a href="mailto:support@brightmoney.co" style="color: inherit; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline; cursor: pointer; ">support@brightmoney.co</a>. We do not hold or control the funds in your Continental Bank deposit account. These funds will be held by Continental Bank for your benefit. In each case, transfers to and from your Continental Bank deposit account will be executed by Continental Bank in accordance with the instructions you provide through the App.
